gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[CRPF Director General GP Singh congratulated personnel on the milestone, saying the last operational death in the force was recorded on October 30, 2025. The previous time the CRPF went such a long period without an operational fatality was before January 1979. The milestone comes against the backdrop of another serious challenge facing the force, the rising number of personnel dying by suicide.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/first-in-47-years-crpf-completes-12-months-without-any-operational-casualties/articleshow/135466441.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/first-in-47-years-crpf-completes-12-months-without-any-operational-casualties/articleshow/135466441.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-02T21:26:53+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135467001,imgsize-112294.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['NCP united under Sunetra Pawar': Party rejects rift rumours as she skips Amit Shah meet]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ncp-united-under-sunetra-pawar-party-rejects-rift-rumours-as-she-skips-amit-shah-meet/articleshow/135465912.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135465912.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The speculation was fuelled by the absence of Maharashtra deputy chief minister Sunetra Pawar and her sons, Parth and Jay, from Sunday's meeting with Shah. The development raised questions about whether the party's leadership was being sidelined in discussions over its future following the death of Ajit Pawar. NCP national chief spokesperson Umesh Patil rejected reports as "incorrect, baseless and misleading".]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ncp-united-under-sunetra-pawar-party-rejects-rift-rumours-as-she-skips-amit-shah-meet/articleshow/135465912.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ncp-united-under-sunetra-pawar-party-rejects-rift-rumours-as-she-skips-amit-shah-meet/articleshow/135465912.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-02T20:54:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135466359,imgsize-105196.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Surge in popularity after reality show': Tej Pratap Yadav asks for enhanced security from Centre]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/surge-in-popularity-after-reality-show-tej-pratap-yadav-asks-for-enchaned-security-from-centre/articleshow/135465350.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135465350.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a post on X, Yadav said his recent appearance on a reality show had increased his popularity, with large numbers of people approaching him in public places to take photographs. He said the crowds posed a risk not only to him but also to the lone security personnel currently assigned to him.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/surge-in-popularity-after-reality-show-tej-pratap-yadav-asks-for-enchaned-security-from-centre/articleshow/135465350.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/surge-in-popularity-after-reality-show-tej-pratap-yadav-asks-for-enchaned-security-from-centre/articleshow/135465350.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-02T20:17:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135465626,imgsize-93652.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Cyclone Murusu: 19 flights cancelled, NDRF on standby as coastal states brace for severe storm - top development]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cyclone-murusu-19-flights-cancelled-ndrf-on-standby-as-coastal-states-brace-for-severe-storm-top-development/articleshow/135465378.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135465378.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cyclone-murusu-19-flights-cancelled-ndrf-on-standby-as-coastal-states-brace-for-severe-storm-top-development/articleshow/135465378.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cyclone-murusu-19-flights-cancelled-ndrf-on-standby-as-coastal-states-brace-for-severe-storm-top-development/articleshow/135465378.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-02T20:07:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135465453,imgsize-1495231.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Cyclone Murasu to make landfall near at Andhra coast tonight; 120 kmph winds expected]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cyclone-murasu-to-make-landfall-near-at-andhra-coast-tonight-120-kmph-winds-expected/articleshow/135464816.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135464816.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Cyclone Murasu has intensified and is predicted to cross the south Andhra Pradesh coast soon. It is expected to bring strong winds reaching up to 120 kmph and heavy rainfall. Several districts in Andhra Pradesh will experience severe weather conditions due to the cyclone. Precautionary measures have been implemented, including rescue operations and evacuation arrangements. Fishermen have been advised to avoid venturing into the sea during this period.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cyclone-murasu-to-make-landfall-near-at-andhra-coast-tonight-120-kmph-winds-expected/articleshow/135464816.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cyclone-murasu-to-make-landfall-near-at-andhra-coast-tonight-120-kmph-winds-expected/articleshow/135464816.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-02T19:49:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aryan Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135464978,imgsize-151612.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Azam the, Azam hain': Will the Khan factor help or haunt Akhilesh in 2027 UP elections?]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/azam-the-azam-hain-will-the-khan-factor-help-or-haunt-akhilesh-in-2027-up-elections/articleshow/135462603.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135462603.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Akhilesh Yadav's recent visit to Azam Khan in jail underscores their deep political connection amidst ongoing legal troubles. Following Azam's fleeting bail, the Enforcement Directorate swiftly took him back into custody, adding complexity to the Samajwadi Party's election preparations. Balancing support for Azam while appealing to Muslim constituents presents a significant challenge for Akhilesh as he navigates potential electoral repercussions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/azam-the-azam-hain-will-the-khan-factor-help-or-haunt-akhilesh-in-2027-up-elections/articleshow/135462603.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/azam-the-azam-hain-will-the-khan-factor-help-or-haunt-akhilesh-in-2027-up-elections/articleshow/135462603.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-02T18:52:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pallavi</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135462853,imgsize-107632.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Your social media posts amounted to instigation': Bombay HC pulls up actor Imran Khan - top quotes]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/your-social-media-posts-amounted-to-instigation-bombay-hc-pulls-up-actor-imran-khan-top-quotes/articleshow/135462621.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135462621.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[A bench comprising Chief Justice Mahesh Chandra Tripathi and Justice Advait Sethna remarked that instead of deporting Khan immediately, authorities had shown leniency by issuing him a notice asking him to leave the country. Khan's lawyer, Venkatesh Dhond, responded by submitting an undertaking that the 43-year-old actor would not participate in any protest in the future. He also conveyed Khan's unconditional apology to the court.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/your-social-media-posts-amounted-to-instigation-bombay-hc-pulls-up-actor-imran-khan-top-quotes/articleshow/135462621.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/your-social-media-posts-amounted-to-instigation-bombay-hc-pulls-up-actor-imran-khan-top-quotes/articleshow/135462621.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-02T18:42:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135463498,imgsize-150102.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Rahul Gandhi has no vision, will be responsible for Congress's wipeout': BJP's Nitin Nabin at anti-SIR march]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rahul-has-no-vision-will-be-responsible-for-congs-wipeout-bjps-nitin-nabin-at-anti-sir-march/articleshow/135462507.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135462507.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rahul-has-no-vision-will-be-responsible-for-congs-wipeout-bjps-nitin-nabin-at-anti-sir-march/articleshow/135462507.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rahul-has-no-vision-will-be-responsible-for-congs-wipeout-bjps-nitin-nabin-at-anti-sir-march/articleshow/135462507.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-02T18:25:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Kanchan Yadav</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135462857,imgsize-99401.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['3 crore Bangladeshi infiltrators don't exist on voters' list': Amit Shah counters Rahul's anti-SIR pitch]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/3-crore-bangladeshi-infiltrators-dont-exist-on-voters-list-amit-shah-counters-rahuls-anti-sir-pitch/articleshow/135460369.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135460369.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a verbal blitzkrieg, a day after Rahul's mega Ramlila Maidan rally in the national capital, Shah said that behind the Congress's criticism of the Special Intensive Revision (SIR) lies an "attempt to protect illegal Bangladeshi infiltrators", three crore of whom, he claimed, were struck off the electoral rolls during the revision.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/3-crore-bangladeshi-infiltrators-dont-exist-on-voters-list-amit-shah-counters-rahuls-anti-sir-pitch/articleshow/135460369.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/3-crore-bangladeshi-infiltrators-dont-exist-on-voters-list-amit-shah-counters-rahuls-anti-sir-pitch/articleshow/135460369.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-